      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HARRY THE HAT (4) has been freshened since a midfield finish in the Triad Final back in August. Was racing very well with a string of top-two finishes prior. Looks well placed so has strong claims, FAN THE FLAME (3) registered a well-deserved maiden victory last start when she led and went on to score by 5.4 metres at Redcliffe. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Leading hope. TASK AT HAND (1) was in the betting but broke and finished a long last on debut. Should enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position so is worth another chance. ILLBERIDINGSHOTGUN (7) broke when resuming but was consistent last time in. Draws wide but will be fitter so worth another chance.",
